# What the Docker image gets: only what the studio runs (an allow-list), never footage, renders, data, keys or the
# working files in public/mezz (which can reach 100+ GB). Dockerfile and docs/self-host.md.
*

!package.json
!package-lock.json
!remotion.config.ts
!tsconfig.json
!LICENSE
!NOTICE
!CHANGELOG.md
!README.md
!server/
!src/
!scripts/
!shared/
!luts/
!examples/
!public/fonts/
!public/geo/
!py/studio/
!py/requirements-linux.lock
!py/requirements-linux-arm64.lock
!docs/*.md
!docs/openapi.yaml

# Inside the folders above: never keys, logs, caches, or the original workspace's own files (not in a public clone).
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/secrets
**/*.log
**/youtube_client.json
**/client_secret*.json
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/node_modules
shared/reels.json
shared/words.json
shared/profiles
examples/public
